    </processinfo>
    <bioghist id="aspace_401809089dbec51d9662e13ae989ef7f">
      <head>Biographical History</head>
      <p>Max Barth was born in Waldkirch in Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany. He was a poet, writer, and journalist. Barth founded his own small weekly newspaper, <emph render="italic">The Direction</emph>.</p>
    </bioghist>
    <scopecontent id="aspace_53ce03cccf71554ad8740cc44c303447">
      <head>Scope and Contents</head>
      <p>Photocopies of handcorrected typescripts of poetry, 1916-1940; and offprints of articles, 1961-1962.</p>
    </scopecontent>
    <arrangement id="aspace_2e2cd16a96118b37614583b433eeaf77">
      <head>Arrangement of the Collection</head>
      <p>The collection has no series.</p>
    </arrangement>
    <acqinfo id="aspace_a0b3fa508e57f10578a80c35d37ca895">
      <head>Acquisition Information</head>
      <p>All items in this manuscript group were donated to the University Libraries, M.E. Grenander Department of Special Collections and Archives.</p>
    </acqinfo>
